unty"],["ARC or PLC in Washington County","/arc-plc/oregon/washington-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Washington County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 40 of 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 33% of normal in June to July and 49% in May to June. July to August is the driest pair at 1.49 inches normal, and November to December is the wettest at 15.46. Grid 30329 had its driest year in 1985 at 63% of normal.</p>"}
